-2026-draft.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"11/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"F.773 - Annex C - Capital Programme","url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39164/f-773-annex-c-capital-programme.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"12/03/2026","key":true},{"title":"F.773 - Annex B - Q3 Budget Virement","url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39163/f-773-annex-b-q3-budget-virement.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"12/03/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Full Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-29","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-19","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-03","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-09","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Full Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Forest of Dean council improves forecast but faces \u00a33.3m five-year funding gap","lead":"Forest of Dean Council's medium-term financial strategy (MTFS), the council's financial plan for the next three to five years, shows a forecast funding gap of approximately \u00a33.3 million over five years to 2030/31, an improvement from the \u00a34.6 million gap identified previously. The council achieved a balanced budget for 2025/26, but the local government auditor's annual report notes the council will face a funding gap from 2027/28 onwards. The auditor says the council will need further savings, transformation activity and income generation to ensure long-term financial sustainability.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"F.794 Annex B FoDDC Agreed Actions Sept 2026","paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39771/39771.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Forest of Dean faces \u00a33.3m funding gap over five years, auditor warns","lead":"Forest of Dean District Council must find significant savings and business transformation to close a cumulative funding gap of approximately \u00a33.3 million over the five years to 2030/31, according to the external auditor's annual report on the 2025/26 accounts. The council improved its position from a previously forecast \u00a34.6 million gap, and achieved a balanced budget for 2026/27, but the auditor notes the council will face a projected funding gap again from 2027/28 onwards. The auditor stated that \"further savings, transformation activity and income generation will be required to ensure long-term financial sustainability.\" The findings come as the council navigates structural changes from the government's Local Government Reorganisation announcement affecting Gloucestershire.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"F.794 Annex B FoDDC Agreed Actions Sept 2026","paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39771/39771.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"FoD Audit Completion Report 2025-26 - 09092026 for papers","paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39792/39792.pdf","headline":"Debtors schedule format causing audit delays; recurring issue from prior year","detail":"Auditor required additional follow-up work because the initial debtors schedule showed brought-forward figures rather than clear year-end position. This is the second year this issue has occurred. Auditor also needed additional supporting evidence for bad debt provision calculation. Management acknowledges it needs improvement and will review in next interim audit.","category":"audit","matters":"Recurring difficulty in producing clear debtors reporting suggests weaknesses in the council's financial systems and control environment. It raises questions about management's visibility of receivables and the reliability of financial reporting processes.","figures":"Issue recurring from 2024/25; no specific monetary values identified","quote":"These included obtaining an appropriate schedule for debtors and obtaining supporting evidence for the calculation of the bad debt provision.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"FoD Audit Completion Report 2025-26 - 09092026 for papers","paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39792/39792.pdf","headline":"Deputy Director of Finance moved to part-time; auditor flags for monitoring in next audit cycle","detail":"Key finance officer transitioned to part-time role. Auditor noted concerns but states arrangements being made for additional support. No issues this year. However auditor explicitly flags this for reconsideration when 'compression of audit timetable next year' is factored in.","category":"people","matters":"Senior finance staff capacity directly affects the council's financial management capability, control environment and financial reporting reliability\u2014all factors lenders assess when making lending decisions.","figures":"One Deputy Director of Finance position reduced to part-time","quote":"There were some concerns regarding the areas in which the Deputy Director of Finance is now part time however there have been conversations regarding another member of staff supporting in this area. However, this has not caused us any issues, with compression of the audit timetable next year this need to be considered.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"FoD Audit Completion Report 2025-26 - 09092026 for papers","paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39792/39792.pdf","headline":"LGPS pension deficit swung to \u00a312.2m from \u00a31.6m, primarily from IFRIC 14 accounting treatment of pension asset","detail":"Pension valuation changed from \u00a31.6m deficit to \u00a312.2m deficit including unfunded obligations. Primary driver: IFRIC 14 accounting removed \u00a325.6m previously recognized pension asset and created \u00a310.7m liability for past service costs, which the council prepaid (\u00a32.459m) post-year-end. Discount rate improved from 5.8% to 6.2%, mechanically reducing the liability.","category":"reserves","matters":"Pension liabilities materially affect the council's reserve position, financial flexibility and borrowing capacity. The post-year-end prepayment of \u00a32.459m represents a cash commitment. A lender needs to understand whether the council's financial position has genuinely changed or whether this is technical restatement.","figures":"Deficit moved from \u00a31.6m (2024/25) to \u00a312.2m (2025/26); IFRIC 14 effect: asset removal \u00a325.6m, liability addition \u00a310.7m; post-balance sheet prepayment \u00a32.459m; discount rate improvement 5.8% to 6.2%","quote":"The pension valuation on the LGPS has moved from a net deficit position of \u00a31.6m to a deficit position of \u00a312.2m, including the effect of the unfunded obligations.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"FoD Audit Completion Report 2025-26 - 09092026 for papers","paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39792/39792.pdf","headline":"Local Government Reorganisation announced on 16 July 2026, affecting Gloucestershire councils including Forest of Dean","detail":"Post-balance sheet event disclosed in financial statements. LGR is a structural governance change affecting the council's future operations, funding, staffing and service delivery. The exact effects are disclosed within the statements.","category":"governance","matters":"LGR creates material uncertainty about the council's future structure and operations, directly affecting a lender's assessment of the council's stability, funding trajectory and ability to service borrowing.","figures":"Announcement date 16 July 2026; post-balance sheet event requiring disclosure","quote":"On 16 July 2026, the government announced their decision in relation to Local Government Reorganisation. A disclosure of this fact and the effects on the Council as part the decision across Gloucestershire has been required to be included within the financial statements.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"HPS.176 Strategic Risk Register - September 2026 Resized","paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39789/39789.pdf","headline":"\u00a3600k Publica cost increase and 95% flat cash settlement require efficiency savings and reserve funding for LGR contribution.","detail":"Following the Publica rebasing exercise, FODDC costs increased by \u00a3600k. The council received a 95% cash flat settlement for 26/27 through to 28/29. To manage this, the council is identifying efficiency savings and will fund its contribution to the LGR Glos budget from reserves.","category":"savings","matters":"A lender would care that budget pressures are forcing reserve depletion and require the council to deliver efficiency savings, both of which reduce financial resilience.","figures":"\u00a3600k cost increase from Publica rebasing; 95% cash flat settlement for 26/27 through to 28/29","quote":"following the Publica rebasing exercise, FODDC costs have increased by circa \u00a3600k. Work is underway to identify potential efficiency savings to bridge this gap. There is also an expectation for FODDC to contribute towards the LGR Glos budget, which will need to be funded from reserves.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Forest of Dean","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-21","since_iso":"2026-08-22","distress":false,"headline":"Debtors schedule format causing audit delays; recurring issue from prior year","lead":"Recurring difficulty in producing clear debtors reporting suggests weaknesses in the council's financial systems and control environment. It raises questions about management's visibility of receivables and the reliability of financial reporting processes.","also":["22 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":23,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"FoD Audit Completion Report 2025-26 - 09092026 for papers","top_paper_url":"https://meetings.fdean.gov.uk/documents/s39792/39792.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":76,"news_drafts_total":2}}